    <string name="txt_instructions" translatable="false"><![CDATA[
        <b>Main feature:</b><br>
        Private DNS Switcher (PDNSS) requires a special Android permission to modify Private DNS settings.<br><br>
        To grant the permission via ADB:<br>
        1. Enable Developer Options<br>
        2. Enable USB debugging<br>
        3. Connect your smartphone to a PC with ADB installed<br>
        4. Allow USB debugging from the PC on your phone<br>
        5. Open a terminal / shell on the PC<br>
        6. Run the command:<br>
        <code>adb shell pm grant com.rudyii.pdnss android.permission.WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS</code><br><br>
        <b>Optional features:</b><br>
        PDNSS can also switch Private DNS automatically based on Trusted Wi-Fi APs, Cellular Network, or VPN state using system network callbacks.
    ]]></string>
    <string name="txt_instructions_title">PDNSS requirements:</string>
    <string name="txt_location_disclosure_title">Location permission disclosure</string>
    <string name="txt_location_disclosure_agreement" translatable="false"><![CDATA[
        <b>This App needs Your location permission in the background to enable the Trusted WiFi AP functionality.</b><br>
        This is an Android requirement to detect trusted Wi-Fi networks.<br><br>
        <b>Granting permission allows You to:</b><br>
        <b>- </b>Trust or untrust currently connected Wi-Fi access points based on their names. Denying permission disables the Trusted WiFi AP functionality. You can always revisit this prompt later to enable it.<br><br>
        <u>Here\'s how Your location is used:</u><br>
        <b>- In the background:</b><br>
        This App uses Your location in the background to identify nearby Wi-Fi networks and check their AP names against Your trusted list. This functionality is not used for any other purpose.<br><br>
        <b>This App does not use Your location data for advertising.</b>
    ]]></string>
